Pros:
- beauteful surroundings;
- rich story;
- visually appealing combat;
- definetely AAA game.
Cons:
- crappy PC version: camera, UI navigation (menu-submenu-submenu and then all way back to close instead of quick keys for everything, we have 102 keys ALT/CTRL/SHIFT for reason), no intro skip, checkpoint saving without way to go back;
- "corridor-alike" gameplay, exploring is not rewarding, nor you can go somewhere away;
- non-skippable LOUD intros (it ignores in-game sound volume settings, literally BLOWING with that "NVIDIA" intro upon launch and I am ATI fan tbh), I know advertisemens are must, but making them this way deserves a sweet hit into balls.. at least;
- acrobatic is overrated, really, there is no need to have so much, it's easy, but time-consuming, coupled with crappy camera it makes gameplay more like annoying.
P.S.: threat this as a first impression, but it's definetely agains finishing this game of spending at least 5 more minutes with it. Not recommended for PC users.

Unfortunately I cannot recommend this adventure game. It has good graphics and puzzles, but there are a lot of technical issues:
- Achievements are not working. I've managed to get 2... But it was just luck;
- Loading is taking a lot of time even on SSD. It's a 2D game with 3D characters and it's taking a while to go from one room to another. As far as it's an adventure and most of the time you just jumping from one location to another it's starting to annoy very soon;
- You cannot skip most of the dialogs. When you left click the subtitles will disappear, but the character keeps talking. It's slowing down the walkthrough to hear dialogs for second time or more (for example to see different options);
- Most of the puzzles are very easy, it's unlikely that you'll stuck somewhere more than for 5 minutes;
- Bugs... tons of them... seriously, the first bug I've faced in the very first room. Mouse got broken and I was not able to get out of the cell. So I've started new game...
The game is 3 years old, so it's unlikely it will get any further support. It's a pity. The game itself is very promising.

What can i say about this game;
It has the likeness of minecraft and rust, plain and simple, so im going to use minecraft/rust as an indirect comparison.
Remember before you even think about buying this game that it is early alpha and the developers aka nerdkingdom do not to my knowledge have any releases of any games under their belt, they are backed and supported by feedthebeast so based on this im giving them a moderate to low risk of getting a game thats not finished and thrown together.
Disclaimer;
As your reading this you may think this game is not for you or maybe im giving it a negative review in writing but recommending it anyway. My review is based on the current state of the game and will likely not reflect some if not all of the finished product and will only probably be relevent for the near future of the games development.
(This is quite a long review so if you cant be bothered reading on ive included a overview at the bottom)
Gameplay;
You play as what i would describe as an elvin creature who has been dumped on a proceeduraly generated world (using the famous world seed system) there are numberous different resourses available to you and a crafting tech tree that can be progressed up.
At the moment it is fairly easy to survive the "energy" (food meter) is easy to fill and once you have found an apple or orange tree you will never go hungry again. Additionally the AI is clunky and stupid, the only time your in trouble from them is in wide open spaces as they like to run into walls wherre you can stand just out of range and kill them.
Additionally your own navigation is hindered by just 1 block height (explains the clunky ai) meaning getting out of your mine takes a lot of jumping and a bit of patience (Yes minecraft does this too but you dont slip back down again)
Mining;
Most of your resources for level 1 tech tree and any basic building material can be found lying around across the entire map, but the tools currently are unbalanced with the pickaxe and the hammer doing the job to quickly and of course the shovel doing the job to slowly and higher level tech tree ores are very rare and hard to find a few balancing issues then here but that particular feature is fresh out of the box.
Building;
The building aspect of this game definately needs some work and you wont be building mega structures just yet as block placement i find is a little bit fiddely, but on the bright side anything you build does come together nicely with the textures all blending seemlessly together.
Mod Support;
Yes im giving this its own section because it remarkable at how easily modded this game is in fact it pretty much has about the same or better mod support than a lot of games out there. For an early alpha thats impressive.
You wont see that many mods yet but i believe they will come strong and fast as just looking at the way mods are imported into the game it seems remarkably too good to be true.
Graphics;
Not much to say here compared to rust and minecraft I would say they are miles better.
Overview;
If you like minecraft or rust and want to support a game that has soo much potential to be better than both of them then for $9.99 or £6.00ish  you really are not risking a lot of money by buying early alpha and with the developers letting us know the price is due to rise as more features are imported into the game, it really is a great time to invest in this game.
I look at the review above and think to myself it really looks quite negative but trust me providing you remember that it is an alpha you wont care about that. With multiplayer support on its way im looking forward to loading this game backup again once the multiplayer support is added.
For those of you interested in a polished off game with as many features as minecraft, alls i have to say is wait for a later beta or final release.

